{"id": "EUVD-2026-101056", "enisaUuid": "f1f8fb11-af9d-3aec-a4d1-bc49edf93f68", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: rsi: fix heap OOB write on key removal\n\nWhen a key is removed (data == NULL), rsi_hal_load_key() runs:\n\n\tmemset(&set_key[FRAME_DESC_SZ], 0, frame_len - FRAME_DESC_SZ);\n\nset_key is a struct rsi_set_key *, so the subscript is scaled by\nsizeof(struct rsi_set_key) (160 bytes): &set_key[FRAME_DESC_SZ] is\nskb->data + 2560, and the memset writes 144 zero bytes starting\n2.4KB past the end of the 160-byte skb data buffer, corrupting\nunrelated heap objects. The intended byte offset would have been\n(u8 *)set_key + FRAME_DESC_SZ.\n\nThe write fires on every DISABLE_KEY callback, so plain disconnects,\nroams and interface teardowns trigger it on real networks.\n\nThe memset is redundant: the whole buffer is zeroed right after\nallocation, so the frame sent to the device is byte-identical\nwithout it. Drop the else branch; normal operation is unaffected.\n\nDiscovered by Atuin - Automated Vulnerability Discovery Engine.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:27:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:00", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b79e2f6585c014c42384f4caa7a37b3e5d26179c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c67fb3b875a83f9ba92afea4036c7b541f77512a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/62d40db89180cfab7a917395f9ffc1dac62b0019", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/00bea3589255603c38766cac4a4d6d36493b2556", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac599cf8edf8aa2dae546f04d3f1849e32c2e738", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f4f2852b664c3ff1436785cd11258a0ce25b74b3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8dab6ee020b2cd951b670626ba44a95cd4deac3d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e6c5ed7a98d7bc8b0f7918246f1c90ddb3f79dfa"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5p9q-rqwh-2www", "CVE-2026-98407"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "16f636cf-0657-3cac-b83e-757b0778926c", "product": {"name"